1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,280
Matthew 23

2
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:06,420
Then Jesus said to the crowds and to his disciples,

3
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:10,520
The scribes and the Pharisees sit on Moses' seat.

4
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:15,320
So practice and observe whatever they tell you, but not what they do.

5
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,120
For they preach, but do not practice.

6
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:23,640
They tie up heavy burdens hard to bear, and lay them on people's shoulders,

7
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:27,800
but they themselves are not willing to move them with their finger.

8
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:31,900
They do all their deeds to be seen by others,

9
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:35,840
for they make their phylacteries broad and their fringes long,

10
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:41,660
and they love the place of honor at feasts, and the best seats in the synagogues,

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,220
and greetings in the marketplaces, and being called rabbi by others.

12
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:52,500
But you are not to be called rabbi, for you have one teacher, and you are all brothers.

13
00:00:52,860 --> 00:00:57,280
And call no man your father on earth, for you have one Father,

14
00:00:57,540 --> 00:00:57,780
who is God.

15
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:03,800
Neither be called instructors, for you have one instructor, the Christ.

16
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:06,600
The greatest among you shall be your servant.

17
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:12,560
Whoever exalts himself will be humbled, and whoever humbles himself will be exalted.

18
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:18,340
But woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites!

19
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:22,080
For you shut the kingdom of heaven in people's faces.

20
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:27,740
For you neither enter yourselves, nor allow those who would enter to go in.

21
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:32,920
Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites!

22
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:38,840
For you travel across sea and land to make a single proselyte,

23
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:44,720
and when he becomes a proselyte, you make him twice as much a child of hell as yourselves.

24
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:48,760
Woe to you, blind guides, who say,

25
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:51,820
If anyone swears by the temple, it is nothing.

26
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:56,820
But if anyone swears by the gold of the temple, he is bound by his oath.

27
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:00,060
You blind fools!

28
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:05,720
For which is greater, the gold or the temple that has made the gold sacred?

29
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:07,760
And you say,

30
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:10,940
If anyone swears by the altar, it is nothing.

31
00:02:11,260 --> 00:02:15,960
But if anyone swears by the gift that is on the altar, he is bound by his oath.

32
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:18,840
You blind men!

33
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:24,200
For which is greater, the gift or the altar that makes the gift sacred?

34
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:27,780
So whoever swears by the altar,

35
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:31,020
swears by it and by everything on it.

36
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:37,300
And whoever swears by the temple, swears by it and by him who dwells in it.

37
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:41,780
And whoever swears by heaven, swears by the throne of God,

38
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:44,620
and by him who sits upon it.

39
00:02:45,980 --> 00:02:50,280
Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites!

40
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:53,940
For you tithe mint and dill and cumin,

41
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:57,760
and have neglected the weightier matters of the law,

42
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:01,400
justice and mercy and faithfulness.

43
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:06,140
These you ought to have done, without neglecting the others.

44
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:09,360
You blind guides!

45
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:12,600
Straining out a gnat and swallowing a camel?

46
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:17,020
Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites!

47
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:20,200
For you clean the outside of the cup and the plate,

48
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:24,380
but inside they are full of greed and self-indulgence.

49
00:03:25,860 --> 00:03:27,200
You blind Pharisee!

50
00:03:27,780 --> 00:03:30,660
First clean the inside of the cup and the plate,

51
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:33,280
that the outside also may be clean.

52
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:38,080
Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites!

53
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:41,900
For you are like whitewashed tombs,

54
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:44,080
which outwardly appear beautiful,

55
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:49,100
but within are full of dead people's bones and all uncleanness.

56
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:53,300
So you also outwardly appear righteous to others,

57
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:57,460
but within you are full of hypocrisy and lawlessness.

58
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:03,020
Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites!

59
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:06,300
For you build the tombs of the prophets

60
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,840
and decorate the monuments of the righteous,

61
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:09,820
saying,

62
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:12,900
If we had lived in the days of our fathers,

63
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:15,260
we would not have taken part with them

64
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:17,060
in shedding the blood of the prophets.

65
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:20,640
Thus you witness against yourselves

66
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:23,760
that you are sons of those who murdered the prophets.

67
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:26,560
Fill up, then, the measure of your fathers.

68
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:29,580
You serpents!

69
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:31,440
You brood of vipers!

70
00:04:31,980 --> 00:04:34,840
How are you to escape being sentenced to hell?

71
00:04:35,540 --> 00:04:39,200
Therefore I send you prophets and wise men and scribes,

72
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:41,840
some of whom you will kill and crucify,

73
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:44,740
and some you will flog in your synagogues

74
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:46,920
and persecute from town to town,

75
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:51,140
so that on you may come all the righteous blood shed on earth,

76
00:04:51,340 --> 00:04:53,280
from the blood of innocent Abel

77
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:56,240
to the blood of Zechariah the son of Berechiah,

78
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,460
whom you murdered,

79
00:04:57,460 --> 00:04:59,660
between the sanctuary and the altar.

80
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:02,000
Truly I say to you,

81
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:05,380
all these things will come upon this generation.

82
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:08,340
O Jerusalem!

83
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:09,960
Jerusalem!

84
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:12,860
The city that kills the prophets

85
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:15,560
and stones those who are sent to it!

86
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:19,320
How often would I have gathered your children together

87
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:22,460
as a hen gathers her brood under her wings,

88
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:24,360
and you would not!

89
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:26,040
See,

90
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:27,040
your house,

91
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:29,080
is left to you desolate.

92
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,240
For I tell you,

93
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:33,460
you will not see me again,

94
00:05:33,760 --> 00:05:34,960
until you say,

95
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:38,920
Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord.

